{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Hear, O Elohim, my song</b> — a musical poem [piyyut]. The proof is that the heh is joined [to the preceding word] and is pointed with pataḥ." "<b>Hear my song</b> — aloud; and <b>my prayer</b> — in the heart, corresponding to Hannah."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 61, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:24.894530102Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}